---
import AgentChip from './AgentChip.astro';
---
<section class="section bridge" id="context-bridge">
      <div class="container bridge-inner">
        <div class="bridge-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow amber">Context Bridge</p>
          <h2>Hit a usage limit?<br />Keep going in another agent.</h2>
          <p class="sub left">
            Herdbell reads your local session transcript and project files and builds a structured
            continuation prompt. Paste it into another agent and keep working without explaining the whole project again.
          </p>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li><span>1</span>Open Herdbell and select your session.</li>
            <li><span>2</span>Click <b>Generate Context</b>.</li>
            <li><span>3</span>Click <b>Copy Context</b> and paste it into the next agent.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="fine">Runs fully on your Mac, with no AI API calls. How complete the output is depends on what your session transcript and project files contain.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bridge-visual">
          <div class="bridge-flow">
            <AgentChip agent="claude" short />
            <span class="flow-arrow">→</span>
            <AgentChip agent="codex" short />
          </div>
          <div class="context-card">
            <div class="context-head">
              <span>Continuation prompt · saas-web</span>
              <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy>Copy Context</button>
            </div>
<pre class="context-body" id="context-text"><span class="h">## Goal</span>
Ship the marketing site + pricing page for a SaaS app.

<span class="h">## Completed</span>
- Hero, features grid, footer components
- Stripe checkout route in /api/checkout

<span class="h">## Key decisions</span>
- Next.js App Router, Tailwind, no UI kit
- Lifetime plan only; no subscriptions

<span class="h">## Open issues</span>
- Navbar overlaps on &lt; 380px widths

<span class="h">## Next steps</span>
1. Build the pricing cards
2. Wire "Buy" to /api/checkout
3. Run the e2e tests</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
